1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,560
Students, we have been blessed with cerulean skies. Couldn't have asked for better weather this fine sports day.

2
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:14,160
Remember, demonstrate good sportsmanship, and just have fun out there.

3
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:17,600
Very stirring words. Thank you for that, sir.

4
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,760
And now, the pledge of fair play.

5
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:30,620
The pledge.

6
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,540
We, the proud student body of Katakiri High School.

7
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:37,360
Is it me, or is the press looking a little blue?

8
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:39,040
Yeah, despite his red hair.

9
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:41,120
That contrast is crazy.

10
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:44,120
Looks like both of his arms are still intact.

11
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,960
Hey, good thing it's cool outside, huh?

12
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:50,240
Lots of people are in long sleeves.

13
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,500
Oh, you're right.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,680
Sengoku had a fit when he heard you were fired up for this.

15
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:57,880
Called you a traitor.

16
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,980
Truth be told, I think this kind of stuff is boring.

17
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,960
I never had a reason to try before.

18
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:12,420
But, this year I'll actually have to put in effort.

19
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:13,760
To beat you.

20
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:18,780
Now, without further ado, let the Katakiri High School sports day begin!

21
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:32,580
Now, without further ado, let's see.

22
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:35,580
意味をくれたこと

23
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:39,880
きっと知らないだろう

24
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:43,680
君が呼ぶ僕の名前

25
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:46,580
由来より大きな

26
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:50,580
意味をくれたこと

27
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:55,580
飲み干した甘いサイダー

28
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:58,580
見せかえる僕を笑った

29
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:05,580
作った笑顔なんかもいらないね

30
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:08,580
どうしてどうして

31
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:14,580
もらってばかりいる僕を

32
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:18,580
愛しいというの

33
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:23,580
僕は何を返して返して

34
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:29,580
生きて生きるんだろうか

35
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:36,580
淡しい想いが満ちていく

36
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:42,580
この感情の名前をそっと

37
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:46,580
君に伝うよ

38
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:51,580
それを渡して

39
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:55,580
Right off the bat, the East and West are neck and neck.

40
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:59,580
No doubt the second-year girls' hurdle had everyone sweating.

41
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:01,580
Any thoughts, Mr. Nakamine?

42
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:02,580
It was insane.

43
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:06,580
Yeah, it was! Second-year ladies came to represent!

44
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:09,580
So, the third-year teams are running the hurdle race next, right?

45
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:10,580
Yep, yep.

46
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:12,580
It's go time!

47
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:15,580
Have fun, but safety first.

48
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:16,580
Yay!

49
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:21,580
Since you have legs, and I'm partnerless for the three-legged race,

50
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:23,580
what do you say we team up, huh?

51
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:25,580
Sign up for Top of the Pole while you're at it.

52
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,580
The East is short one guy.

53
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,580
I would rather be a shellfish right now.

54
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,580
Next up is a third-year girls' hurdle race.

55
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,580
Well, I gotta run.

56
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:37,580
Go and kick all the bats!

57
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,580
I didn't realize you were racing, too.

58
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:47,580
I bet that you're super-duper quick, aren't you?

59
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:49,580
Nah, I'd say I'm average at best.

60
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:51,580
Yeah, right, like I believe that.

61
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:53,580
I shall mow down any who stand in my way!

62
00:03:53,580 --> 00:03:55,580
You've got this!

63
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,580
You do!

64
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:58,580
The best is the best!

65
00:03:58,580 --> 00:03:59,580
Hear that?

66
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:02,580
Miyamoto's cheering his heart out for Remy to win!

67
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:05,580
I believe that he's cheering for the entirety of the West team.

68
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:07,580
Next team, line up!

69
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:12,580
Since he's watching, I'm gonna work extra hard.

70
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,580
Yeah, um, he wasn't cheering just for you.

71
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:17,580
If Remy wins, Miyamoto belongs to her.

72
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:19,580
K, Kion, Kion!

73
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:20,580
Uh, Kion?

74
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:21,580
What?

75
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:22,580
Get set!

76
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:24,580
Hey!

77
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:26,580
Ayasaki's fast!

78
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:27,580
He's a dark horse?

79
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:28,580
He wants!

80
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:29,580
Ayasaki is leading!

81
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:30,580
He fights!

82
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:36,580
Oof, that sounded painful.

83
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:38,580
I think she kicked it on purpose.

84
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:39,580
Metal.

85
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:44,580
She said that stuff to get under my skin!

86
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:45,580
Damn it!

87
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:46,580
Look, Mugs!

88
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:48,580
Team East is trailing behind!

89
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,580
Thanks, Captain Obvious!

90
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:53,580
The East girl bringing up the rear is looking really intense.

91
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:56,580
Yeah, you kinda sorta know it.

92
00:04:57,580 --> 00:05:01,580
East takes first, and West takes second!

93
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:05,580
I tell my boyfriend not to slack, then come in dead last.

94
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,580
Man, what is my deal?

95
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:08,580
Huh?

96
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,580
Honey!

97
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,580
Don't give up!

98
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:11,580
Huh?

99
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:12,580
Huh?

100
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:13,580
Huh?

101
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:14,580
Huh?

102
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:15,580
Huh?

103
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:16,580
Huh?

104
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:17,580
Huh?

105
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:18,580
Huh?

106
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:19,580
Huh?

107
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:20,580
Huh?

108
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:21,580
Huh?

109
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:22,580
Huh?

110
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,580
Huh?

111
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:24,580
Huh?

112
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:25,580
Huh?

113
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:26,580
Huh?

114
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:27,580
Huh?

115
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:28,580
She's the enemy!

116
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,580
No cheering!

117
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,580
Finish strong, even if it's last place, okay?

118
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:33,580
Take the bed out of hell!

119
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:36,580
He's kind of burst of speed from nowhere!

120
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:41,580
Kion Kion!

121
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:44,580
Could you not with the Kion Kion stuff?

122
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:47,580
Because you and Miyamoto are so lovey-dovey with each other,

123
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:50,580
Rami can hardly bear the thought of stealing him away!

124
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:52,580
Freakin' puppet master!

125
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:53,580
Just kidding!

126
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:55,580
Rami's heart belongs to Sengoku!

127
00:05:55,580 --> 00:05:59,580
You just get blustered so easily, but it's really adorable!

128
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:00,580
Now listen, you!

129
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:01,580
Hey!

130
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:02,580
There you are!

131
00:06:02,580 --> 00:06:03,580
Got a sec?

132
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:05,580
Did I interrupt you?

133
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:06,580
We're through!

134
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:07,580
So I'll be going now!

135
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:09,580
I'll even take your sign!

136
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:10,580
Oh!

137
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:11,580
Nice!

138
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,580
Is your leg okay?

139
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,580
That hurdle race was impressive!

140
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,580
It was last place!

141
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:20,580
You looked like a regular pro during your practice sessions,

142
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,580
but then you stalled out for the real thing!

143
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:23,580
Why?

144
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:24,580
Because of you!

145
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:25,580
That's why!

146
00:06:25,580 --> 00:06:26,580
Wait!

147
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:28,580
Then why'd you speed up at the end?

148
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:29,580
That was also your fault!

149
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:30,580
I'm confused!

150
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:31,580
And I'm gonna watch the next race!

151
00:06:31,580 --> 00:06:32,580
You should make your way back too!

152
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:33,580
Okay!

153
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,580
Before you go...

154
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:35,580
Thanks...

155
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:36,580
For cheering...

156
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:37,580
Made me happy!

157
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,580
Sure!

158
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:39,580
Miyamura!

159
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:40,580
Miyamura!

160
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:42,580
Check it out!

161
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:43,580
Look who's also repping Team West!

162
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:47,580
Can she even lift the tug-of-war rope?

163
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:48,580
Huh?

164
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,580
Oh!

165
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:52,580
Pori-senpai!

166
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:53,580
Watch me compete, okay?

167
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:54,580
She is on the other team, right?

168
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,580
I think so!

169
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:56,580
Go, Sawada!

170
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,540
Look who's also repping Team West.

171
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,820
Can't she even lift the tug-of-war rope?

172
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,840
Party Senpai!

173
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:06,920
Watch me compete, okay?

174
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:09,280
She is on the other team, right?

175
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:09,960
I think so.

176
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:11,920
Go, Sawada!

177
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,540
Give it all you got, girl!

178
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:15,560
Or not.

179
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,540
For a quick second, I thought our cheering was too loud.

180
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:28,220
Dude, who doesn't love having people in their corner?

181
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:30,800
You eat that stuff up too, don't you?

182
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,740
I've never really done the cheer thing on Sports Day.

183
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:36,780
And nobody ever cheered for me.

184
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:41,480
I suggest that you start by cheering more for your team than your opponents, rookie.

185
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,420
I got caught up in the moment.

186
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:44,700
Sorry.

187
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:49,720
Be real nice if you could drown out the other team while I compete in the upcoming obstacle course.

188
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:53,700
If there's one person who won't snub you for cheering loud, it's your boy.

189
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:55,140
Right.

190
00:07:55,540 --> 00:08:01,760
I tried so hard, but the West team lost.

191
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,660
Hey, don't let it get you down.

192
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:06,200
There were a whole bunch of jocks on Team East's side.

193
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:10,260
I wanted you to see me emerge victorious and look cool!

194
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:12,860
Take your cheers off Team East, sirf.

195
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:17,740
Ishikawa is next stop.

196
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:19,060
Cheer really loud!

197
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:34,540
I wish I were on the West side.

198
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:36,620
My team sounds like they'll kill me.

199
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:37,760
Where's the prez?

200
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,760
Said he was only participating in the mandatory stuff.

201
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,840
Now on your marks...

202
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,000
Get set!

203
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:50,180
And the fellas are off to brave the obstacle course.

204
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:54,960
First up is the balance beam, and neither team is ready to give up the lead just yet.

205
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:57,460
Ishikawa, keep going!

206
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,080
Go away!

207
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,880
Go away, Ishikawa!

208
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:00,560
Run!

209
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:01,680
All together.

210
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:02,680
Go for gold!

211
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:03,680
Ishikawa!

212
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,060
Go for gold! Ishikawa!

213
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,480
One more.

214
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:09,980
Ready? Stay strong!

215
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:11,520
Nearly there!

216
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:13,520
Oh, calling your name.

217
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,020
Lucky you.

218
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:18,020
Yeah, except there's also one high-pitched guy mixed in.

219
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:20,860
How about that?

220
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:23,700
Finally found your voice.

221
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:27,200
Gosh, which team would pull off the win?

222
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:29,240
Ishikawas!

223
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:32,000
So you two tied?

224
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,300
That's pretty darn good for somebody like Iura, right?

225
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:37,300
Yoshikawa's words, not mine.

226
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:39,100
Though you have my praise as well.

227
00:09:39,180 --> 00:09:42,340
That's praise? Speaking of, where are the girls at?

228
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:43,840
They're getting ready.

229
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,940
It's almost time for the cheer competition.

230
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:47,640
All right, guys!

231
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,980
The moment of pom-poms is upon us!

232
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:52,480
First up, the East Team third years!

233
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:56,320
Say it loud, everyone! Go!

234
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:57,520
East!

235
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:01,800
A-S-T-B-I-K-U!

236
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:02,760
Wee!

237
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,100
Oh, isn't somebody the greatest?

238
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:06,600
Oh, absolutely!

239
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,600
I've never seen a cheer like this before.

240
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,900
That officially makes two of us.

241
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:14,940
I wonder how Kyochan's boyfriend feels watching this unique display.

242
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:16,940
Oh, we lost him.

243
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:18,140
Figures.

244
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:20,060
Take courage, Team West!

245
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:21,320
Ready?

246
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,320
Okay!

247
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,860
Here we go!

248
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:25,240
We're the West!

249
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,660
Win, win, West!

250
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:28,240
No stress, we're best.

251
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:30,700
Put our powers to the best!

252
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:35,700
So Team East was a hit with the girls, and Team West won over the guys.

253
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:37,620
Wasn't that going to be a little too cute?

254
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:39,540
Deep breaths, Fres. Deep breaths.

255
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:42,540
Right, right, bounce and up.

256
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:44,520
Now punch to the left and pose.

257
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:45,980
Fight hard!

258
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,820
Drink big!

259
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,200
I did it.

260
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,200
That was so much fun.

261
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,400
It was so much fun.

262
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:57,540
That was seriously hot stuff.

263
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:59,100
Like, I'm talking sweltering.

264
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:00,280
Right back at ya.

265
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:01,740
You're a star, honey!

266
00:11:01,820 --> 00:11:02,840
Oh, shucks.

267
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:03,840
Yoshikawa!

268
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,440
You rocked it out there, Kono!

269
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:08,780
Your entire team looked fantastic!

270
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:10,160
You really mean it?

271
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:12,160
Thank you.

272
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:15,320
You could've let me struggle all on my own.

273
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:18,220
But you took the time to help me learn the routines.

274
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,960
I should've thanked you sooner, I know.

275
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,140
You missed sincerity over here!

276
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,600
I did mean every word.

277
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,140
Now there's a chance.

278
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:30,280
Ishikawa noticed me in a good way.

279
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:37,500
Dude, you knew it was coming, so what is your deal?

280
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:41,180
I wanted to see her with pom-poms and a skirt.

281
